{"id": "EUVD-2026-103777", "enisaUuid": "5f31cadc-b5e8-331d-a3b4-74f1cdd16c94", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: caiaq: unregister the input device when probe fails\n\nsetup_card() registers the input device, whose name and phys point into\nstruct snd_usb_caiaqdev, and then goes on to snd_card_register() and\nsnd_usb_caiaq_control_init(). If either fails, snd_probe() calls\nsnd_card_free(), which frees the device state but leaves the input\ndevice registered: card_free() only clears the pointer, and the input\ndevice is unregistered from snd_disconnect() alone. Reading its \"uevent\"\nattribute afterwards dereferences freed memory:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in string+0x4a9/0x4f0\n  Read of size 1 at addr ffff8880208f5043 by task caiaq/4967\n   add_uevent_var+0x183/0x3a0\n   input_dev_uevent+0x162/0x900\n   dev_uevent+0x2f1/0x870\n   uevent_show+0x1ca/0x3a0\n   ...\n\nUnregister the input device on the probe error path, as\nsnd_disconnect() does. snd_usb_caiaq_input_disconnect() is a no-op when\nno input device was registered.\n\nReproduced with a raw-gadget Audio Kontrol 1 and a temporary hack that\nmakes snd_usb_caiaq_control_init() fail.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df2787819bd137111b56b8631dd581b0cce7144d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/850810c12686f80cdf7530f4f21e0157d904f739", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84727facd8506140cd04f2b0a8b1c4ddeac41cea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e5a413cc2a489c9427ecd3d73ad764bfb0c7103", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b7bd20f6379bc5e431fd74d866390f5b5b63f3c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98837", "GHSA-gvp5-mg7r-w29g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "191b7892-bd5c-3c8a-8999-434e16ab9656", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "25eabce8-1d5b-3c2d-a2a2-1d47fb6bf8e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.209 <5.16"}, {"id": "26b9956e-6d01-3fd3-9368-8b72637205f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e59ecd4ee3a450db6cb4e4ecaa3efdd593f80056 <84727facd8506140cd04f2b0a8b1c4ddeac41cea"}, {"id": "302aa6ca-95ba-3658-ab3a-08b1037812a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4993be23-25b5-31b9-ae85-3bf362113aab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.140 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "58abc8bf-9295-3901-8691-67aad97308ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28abd224db4a49560b452115bca3672a20e45b2f <2e5a413cc2a489c9427ecd3d73ad764bfb0c7103"}, {"id": "5e2c4bf2-e53a-30a1-a6ab-7815e7af47cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.258 <5.11"}, {"id": "60f05694-f8cb-3341-8d28-86c0623b2989", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "71191103-bc2c-3226-8936-7cfa68f14365", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "76813259-52f7-3f85-ab78-7f23519607b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "78414dd2-8017-3476-8d46-b7e7b107781a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "78e5b3cf-a498-3e7a-a436-959ebf72a6b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "da938aa9fc7826901921dcea225948ab21a97e45"}, {"id": "875a7352-cf4c-38bb-af82-0a9a6b6473ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18.27 <6.18.56"}, {"id": "882aa571-1408-373d-939c-f3cfd17d0a51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0.4 <7.1"}, {"id": "8f12